# Lab 20 Experiment 3A: Create an opaque-source companion with a365 setup all
#
# Question:
# Can the supported Agent 365 CLI create one complete dedicated companion
# stack for an existing Registry Sync source while:
# - leaving the original Registry Sync Package unchanged;
# - accepting the CLI-generated Registration sourceAgentId without rewriting
#   it to the DD-002 companion naming convention; and
# - preserving the provider-to-companion relationship only in durable mapping?
#
# This can run as a paired comparison against Experiment 03 using the same
# approved disposable GCP source. In that mode, the existing deterministic
# companion must be fully created, readable, and mapped, with no unresolved
# write. Experiment 3A deliberately creates a second companion temporarily so
# their source IDs, identity stacks, permissions, and Package representations
# can be compared.
#
# This paired mode is experiment-only. It temporarily violates the normal
# one-active-companion-per-scoped-source invariant and must not be treated as a
# committed-fleet lifecycle design.
#
# Observed verdict:
# The CLI-created Registration had no originatingStore and its Package
# platform was `Not Available`. Because committed-fleet must identify and
# filter companion Registrations by third-party platform, this provisioning
# path is rejected for implementation use.
#
# The only remote write in this experiment is:
#
# a365 setup all --agent-name <synthetic-name> --tenant-id <tenant-id> --authmode obo
#
# Do not send a Graph POST, PATCH, or DELETE from this file. Do not modify the
# sourceAgentId returned by the CLI.
#
# Installed CLI baseline used when this file was written:
# a365 1.1.214+90c444832f
#
# Recheck `a365 --version` and `a365 setup all --help` before running.
#
# Add these values to the shared ignored ../../.env:
#
# A365_EXP3A_TARGET_NAME=<exact-selected-package-display-name>
# A365_EXP3A_PACKAGE_ID=<original-registry-sync-package-id>
# A365_EXP3A_PROVIDER_SOURCE_AGENT_ID=<exact-provider-source-agent-id>
# A365_EXP3A_CLI_AGENT_NAME=<unique-synthetic-cli-agent-name>
# A365_EXP3A_BLUEPRINT_OBJECT_ID=<leave-empty-until-CLI-success>
# A365_EXP3A_BLUEPRINT_APP_ID=<leave-empty-until-CLI-success>
# A365_EXP3A_BLUEPRINT_PRINCIPAL_ID=<leave-empty-until-CLI-success>
# A365_EXP3A_AGENT_IDENTITY_ID=<leave-empty-until-CLI-success>
# A365_EXP3A_CLI_SOURCE_AGENT_ID=<leave-empty-until-registration-readback>
# A365_EXP3A_REGISTRATION_ID=<leave-empty-until-CLI-success>
# A365_EXP3A_COMPANION_PACKAGE_ID=<leave-empty-until-Package-list-readback>
#
# Evidence belongs only under:
# ../../evidence/experiments/03a-cli-setup-all-companion-create/
#
# All saved results must be JSON. Never save authentication responses, access
# tokens, generated credentials, raw CLI setup output, or a generated CLI
# configuration containing credentials.
#
# Run one request or CLI command at a time. Never use "Send All".

@tenantId = {{$dotenv A365_TENANT_ID}}
@clientId = {{$dotenv A365_CLIENT_ID}}
@targetName = {{$dotenv A365_EXP3A_TARGET_NAME}}
@packageId = {{$dotenv A365_EXP3A_PACKAGE_ID}}
@providerSourceAgentId = {{$dotenv A365_EXP3A_PROVIDER_SOURCE_AGENT_ID}}
@blueprintObjectId = {{$dotenv A365_EXP3A_BLUEPRINT_OBJECT_ID}}
@blueprintAppId = {{$dotenv A365_EXP3A_BLUEPRINT_APP_ID}}
@blueprintPrincipalId = {{$dotenv A365_EXP3A_BLUEPRINT_PRINCIPAL_ID}}
@agentIdentityId = {{$dotenv A365_EXP3A_AGENT_IDENTITY_ID}}
@cliSourceAgentId = {{$dotenv A365_EXP3A_CLI_SOURCE_AGENT_ID}}
@registrationId = {{$dotenv A365_EXP3A_REGISTRATION_ID}}
@companionPackageId = {{$dotenv A365_EXP3A_COMPANION_PACKAGE_ID}}
@graphBaseUrl = https://graph.microsoft.com
@readScopes = https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FUser.Read%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FCopilotPackages.Read.All%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentIdentityBlueprint.Read.All%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentIdentityBlueprintPrincipal.Read.All%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentIdentity.Read.All%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentRegistration.Read.All%20offline_access

###############################################################################
# Step 3A.1 - Authenticate for read-only Graph observations
#
# DO NOT SAVE either authentication response or the /me response.

# @name exp3aDeviceCode
POST https://login.microsoftonline.com/{{tenantId}}/oauth2/v2.0/devicecode
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id={{clientId}}&scope={{readScopes}}

###

# Complete browser sign-in before sending this request.

# @name exp3aToken
POST https://login.microsoftonline.com/{{tenantId}}/oauth2/v2.0/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=urn%3Aietf%3Aparams%3Aoauth%3Agrant-type%3Adevice_code&client_id={{clientId}}&device_code={{exp3aDeviceCode.response.body.$.device_code}}

###

# @name exp3aCurrentUser
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/me?$select=id
Authorization: Bearer {{exp3aToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Step 3A.2 - Capture complete Package inventory before CLI setup
#
# Expected: 200. Save the first page as:
#
# ../../evidence/experiments/03a-cli-setup-all-companion-create/package-list-before-page-1.json
#
# Follow every @odata.nextLink and save page-2.json, page-3.json, and so on
# until the latest page has no next link.
#
# Select exactly one approved disposable GoogleVertexAI Package. It may be the
# same source used by Experiment 03 only when that experiment's deterministic
# companion is fully verified and retained as the paired comparison control.
# Copy the original Registry Sync Package's exact displayName and Package ID
# into A365_EXP3A_TARGET_NAME and A365_EXP3A_PACKAGE_ID.

# @name exp3aListPackagesBefore
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages
Authorization: Bearer {{exp3aToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Step 3A.3 - Capture the selected original Registry Sync Package
#
# Expected: 200. Save as:
#
# ../../evidence/experiments/03a-cli-setup-all-companion-create/original-package-before.json
#
# Confirm:
# - id and displayName match Step 3A.2;
# - platform is GoogleVertexAI;
# - agentIdentityId is absent or null; and
# - the nested Connected Platform definition contains the exact provider
#   SourceAgentId.
#
# Copy that exact value byte-for-byte into
# A365_EXP3A_PROVIDER_SOURCE_AGENT_ID. It is the durable mapping key, not the
# sourceAgentId that the CLI will create.

# @name exp3aOriginalPackageBefore
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages/{{packageId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{exp3aToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Step 3A.4 - Choose one unique synthetic CLI agent name
#
# Set A365_EXP3A_CLI_AGENT_NAME to a unique synthetic value. Do not use the
# provider source ID, Package ID, tenant ID, project ID, or another real
# identifier in the name.
#
# The name is not the authoritative relationship. The protected mapping is.
# Do not select an existing CLI agent merely because its display name matches.

###############################################################################
# Step 3A.5 - Inspect the installed CLI and preview the complete setup
#
# From the Lab 20 root, use a fresh PowerShell process. Create an isolated
# ignored workspace first because setup writes project settings:
#
# $labRoot = (Get-Location).Path
# $workspace = Join-Path $labRoot 'evidence\experiments\03a-cli-setup-all-companion-create\cli-workspace'
# New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $workspace | Out-Null
# Set-Location $workspace
# $agentName = Read-Host 'Enter A365_EXP3A_CLI_AGENT_NAME'
# $tenantId = Read-Host 'Enter A365_TENANT_ID'
# a365 --version
# a365 setup all --help
# a365 setup all --agent-name $agentName --tenant-id $tenantId --authmode obo --dry-run
#
# The dry run must plan one Blueprint, one Blueprint principal, permissions,
# one Agent Identity, and one Agent Registration. Current CLI versions can
# additionally plan a client secret, federated identity credential, managed
# identity, default Observability and Power Platform permissions, and a local
# appsettings.json write. Experiment 3A evaluates the complete supported CLI
# bundle, so record these expected companion effects rather than rejecting the
# Registration path merely because setup is not minimal.
#
# Stop if it plans an M365 messaging endpoint, a second Agent Identity, another
# existing agent's objects, or an effect outside the displayed full-setup
# bundle. Continue only with disposable objects and an isolated local
# workspace.
#
# Do not save raw CLI output. Save a manually redacted JSON summary as:
#
# ../../evidence/experiments/03a-cli-setup-all-companion-create/cli-dry-run.json
#
# Use this shape:
#
# {
#   "step": "cli-dry-run",
#   "observedAt": "<UTC-timestamp>",
#   "cliVersion": "<version>",
#   "exitCode": 0,
#   "outcome": "supported",
#   "plannedResourceClasses": [
#     "agent-identity-blueprint",
#     "blueprint-principal",
#     "client-secret",
#     "federated-identity-credential",
#     "managed-identity",
#     "permissions",
#     "agent-identity",
#     "agent-registration",
#     "local-project-settings"
#   ],
#   "unexpectedResourceClasses": [],
#   "safeNotes": "<non-identifying-summary>"
# }

###############################################################################
# Stop 3A-A - approve exactly one CLI full setup
#
# Continue only when:
# - the original Package and exact provider source were captured;
# - protected mapping proves either:
#   - no companion exists; or
#   - exactly one verified Experiment 03 deterministic companion is the
#     explicit paired comparison control;
# - no companion create or cleanup has an unresolved outcome;
# - the synthetic CLI name is unique;
# - the operator accepts the displayed complete CLI bundle, including the
#   managed identity, FIC, client secret, local settings, and default
#   permission configuration;
# - the intended auth mode and permission behavior are recorded;
# - any required administrator action is understood; and
# - one `a365 setup all` attempt is explicitly authorized.
#
# A previous timeout, process interruption, unknown exit, or partial result is
# not permission to run setup again. Reconcile CLI state and Graph objects
# first.

###############################################################################
# Step 3A.6 - Run a365 setup all without customizing sourceAgentId
#
# DO NOT RUN until Stop 3A-A is satisfied.
#
# Reuse the same PowerShell variables and isolated workspace from Step 3A.5:
#
# a365 setup all --agent-name $agentName --tenant-id $tenantId --authmode obo
#
# Do not pass --m365. Do not use --agent-registration-only. Do not patch or
# replace the sourceAgentId selected by the CLI.
#
# Do not redirect or save raw setup output because it can contain generated
# credential material. Store generated credentials only in an approved secret
# store. Keep generated CLI configuration private and untracked.
#
# Save only a redacted JSON status summary as:
#
# ../../evidence/experiments/03a-cli-setup-all-companion-create/cli-setup-result.json
#
# {
#   "step": "cli-setup-all",
#   "observedAt": "<UTC-timestamp>",
#   "exitCode": 0,
#   "outcome": "supported",
#   "createdOrResolved": {
#     "blueprint": true,
#     "blueprintPrincipal": true,
#     "permissions": true,
#     "agentIdentity": true,
#     "agentRegistration": true
#   },
#   "adminActionRequired": false,
#   "safeNotes": "<non-identifying-summary>"
# }
#
# If setup reports partial completion or administrator action, record that
# exact class instead of marking the stack complete.

###############################################################################
# Step 3A.7 - Query CLI permission and inheritance state
#
# Run each command from the same private CLI context:
#
# a365 query-entra blueprint-scopes --agent-name $agentName --tenant-id $tenantId
# a365 query-entra inheritance --agent-name $agentName --tenant-id $tenantId
# a365 query-entra instance-scopes --agent-name $agentName --tenant-id $tenantId
#
# Save each result as a JSON envelope containing the command, exit code,
# outcome class, and redacted output lines:
#
# ../../evidence/experiments/03a-cli-setup-all-companion-create/cli-blueprint-scopes.json
# ../../evidence/experiments/03a-cli-setup-all-companion-create/cli-inheritance.json
# ../../evidence/experiments/03a-cli-setup-all-companion-create/cli-instance-scopes.json
#
# Never record a client secret, token, tenant value, or raw generated config in
# those files.

###############################################################################
# Step 3A.8 - Recover the CLI-created object IDs
#
# Inspect only the CLI-generated private state and the successful setup
# summary. The CLI summary labels the Blueprint application object ID as
# `Blueprint ID`; it does not label separate object-ID and app-ID values.
#
# First copy the exact values that the CLI displayed into the ignored .env:
#
# A365_EXP3A_BLUEPRINT_OBJECT_ID
# A365_EXP3A_BLUEPRINT_PRINCIPAL_ID
# A365_EXP3A_AGENT_IDENTITY_ID
# A365_EXP3A_REGISTRATION_ID
#
# Leave A365_EXP3A_BLUEPRINT_APP_ID empty until Step 3A.9. The fields have
# different meanings even when their returned values happen to be equal.
#
# Do not infer an ID from a display name. If the CLI does not expose one of the
# first four identifiers, record that field as unavailable and do not guess.
#
# The observed CLI-created Registration ID is a GUID and can be used directly
# as a URL path segment. No separate path-encoding variable is required.
# Reload REST Client after updating .env.

###############################################################################
# Step 3A.9 - Verify the CLI-created Blueprint
#
# Expected: 200. Save as:
#
# ../../evidence/experiments/03a-cli-setup-all-companion-create/blueprint-after-cli.json
#
# The response contains both:
# - id: must equal A365_EXP3A_BLUEPRINT_OBJECT_ID; and
# - appId: copy this exact value into A365_EXP3A_BLUEPRINT_APP_ID.
#
# In the CLI 1.1.221 observation, `id`, `appId`, and the CLI summary's
# Blueprint ID were equal. Record both fields independently instead of assuming
# that every Blueprint creation path or future CLI version preserves equality.
#
# Save .env and reload REST Client before Step 3A.10.

# @name exp3aGetBlueprint
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/applications/{{blueprintObjectId}}/microsoft.graph.agentIdentityBlueprint
Authorization: Bearer {{exp3aToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Step 3A.10 - Verify the CLI-created Blueprint principal
#
# Expected: 200. Confirm its id equals A365_EXP3A_BLUEPRINT_PRINCIPAL_ID and
# accountEnabled is not false. Save as:
#
# ../../evidence/experiments/03a-cli-setup-all-companion-create/blueprint-principal-after-cli.json

# @name exp3aGetBlueprintPrincipal
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/servicePrincipals(appId='{{blueprintAppId}}')/microsoft.graph.agentIdentityBlueprintPrincipal
Authorization: Bearer {{exp3aToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Step 3A.11 - Verify the CLI-created Agent Identity
#
# Expected: 200. Confirm agentIdentityBlueprintId equals
# A365_EXP3A_BLUEPRINT_APP_ID. Save as:
#
# ../../evidence/experiments/03a-cli-setup-all-companion-create/agent-identity-after-cli.json

# @name exp3aGetAgentIdentity
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/servicePrincipals/{{agentIdentityId}}/microsoft.graph.agentIdentity
Authorization: Bearer {{exp3aToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Step 3A.12 - Verify the CLI-created Registration
#
# Expected: 200. Save as:
#
# ../../evidence/experiments/03a-cli-setup-all-companion-create/registration-after-cli.json
#
# Copy the returned sourceAgentId exactly into
# A365_EXP3A_CLI_SOURCE_AGENT_ID. Do not rewrite it.
#
# Record whether it equals:
# - the Agent Identity object ID;
# - the Blueprint app ID;
# - the original provider SourceAgentId; or
# - another value.
#
# The expected experiment distinction is that this value does not use the
# DD-002 agent-governance companion namespace.

# @name exp3aGetRegistration
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/beta/copilot/agentRegistrations/{{registrationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{exp3aToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json
OData-Version: 4.0

###

###############################################################################
# Step 3A.13 - List Packages after CLI setup
#
# Expected: 200. Save every page, starting with:
#
# ../../evidence/experiments/03a-cli-setup-all-companion-create/package-list-after-page-1.json
#
# Identify independently:
#
# 1. Original Registry Sync Package:
#    - id equals A365_EXP3A_PACKAGE_ID;
#    - platform is GoogleVertexAI; and
#    - nested source equals A365_EXP3A_PROVIDER_SOURCE_AGENT_ID.
#
# 2. Existing Experiment 03 deterministic companion Package, when paired mode
#    is used:
#    - its source uses the recorded DD-002 companion namespace;
#    - its Blueprint, Agent Identity, Registration, and Package IDs match the
#      Experiment 03 mapping; and
#    - it remains unchanged by the CLI setup.
#
# 3. CLI-created companion Package:
#    - nested source equals A365_EXP3A_CLI_SOURCE_AGENT_ID;
#    - Blueprint and Agent Identity links match the CLI-created objects; and
#    - it is not selected by display name alone.
#
# Put its Package ID into A365_EXP3A_COMPANION_PACKAGE_ID. If no unambiguous
# companion Package is visible, record unavailable or inconclusive and do not
# run setup again.

# @name exp3aListPackagesAfter
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages
Authorization: Bearer {{exp3aToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Step 3A.14 - Confirm the original Registry Sync Package is unchanged
#
# Save as:
#
# ../../evidence/experiments/03a-cli-setup-all-companion-create/original-package-after.json
#
# Before sending, confirm `A365_EXP3A_PACKAGE_ID` exactly equals the `id` saved
# in `original-package-before.json` and that Step 3A.13 contains that ID
# exactly once. If either check fails, do not send this request. Reconcile the
# ignored .env from the saved baseline first.
#
# Expected success is 200. Only after the request target has passed those
# checks may a 424 whose safe error class says that Title Preview could not be
# found be classified as `inconclusive-dependency-failure`.
#
# A saved 424 from an ID that differs from the baseline is an invalid
# observation, not evidence about the original Package. Correct the local ID
# and retry this read once. Do not rerun `a365 setup all`.

# @name exp3aOriginalPackageAfter
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages/{{packageId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{exp3aToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Step 3A.15 - Read the CLI-created companion Package
#
# Save as:
#
# ../../evidence/experiments/03a-cli-setup-all-companion-create/companion-package-after.json

# @name exp3aCompanionPackageAfter
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages/{{companionPackageId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{exp3aToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Step 3A.16 - Save the durable mapping
#
# Save one protected JSON mapping as:
#
# ../../evidence/experiments/03a-cli-setup-all-companion-create/mapping.json
#
# It must contain:
# - the complete scoped provider source key;
# - original Package ID;
# - synthetic CLI agent name;
# - exact CLI-generated sourceAgentId;
# - Registration ID;
# - companion Package ID;
# - Blueprint object ID and app ID;
# - Blueprint principal ID;
# - Agent Identity ID;
# - permission and consent status;
# - CLI version and auth mode;
# - setup start/completion timestamps;
# - status and any unresolved operation; and
# - last verification timestamp.
#
# In paired mode, also record the existing Experiment 03 companion source,
# Registration, Package, Blueprint, and Agent Identity IDs under a separate
# `comparisonControl` object. Mark the 03A mapping `comparison-only`; do not
# replace the normal active mapping for the scoped provider source.
#
# The mapping, not the CLI name or Registration sourceAgentId, is the
# authoritative relationship between the Registry Sync source and this
# companion.

###############################################################################
# Cleanup - optional only after all observations are complete
#
# Do not clean up if this CLI-created companion will be used by a separately
# approved rename, runtime, activity, or lifecycle experiment.
#
# First preview cleanup:
#
# a365 cleanup --agent-name $agentName --tenant-id $tenantId --dry-run
#
# Save a redacted JSON plan as:
#
# ../../evidence/experiments/03a-cli-setup-all-companion-create/cli-cleanup-dry-run.json
#
# Proceed only after the plan identifies exactly this experiment's CLI-created
# objects and cleanup is separately approved. In paired mode it must not
# include the Experiment 03 control Blueprint, Identity, or Registration:
#
# a365 cleanup --agent-name $agentName --tenant-id $tenantId
#
# Save a redacted JSON result as:
#
# ../../evidence/experiments/03a-cli-setup-all-companion-create/cli-cleanup-result.json
#
# Then repeat Steps 3A.9 through 3A.15 as read-only cleanup verification. In
# paired mode, require the Experiment 03 control companion to remain readable
# and unchanged while the CLI-created companion is removed. Do not assume CLI
# exit code 0 proves Registration or Package disappearance. Preserve the 03A
# comparison mapping as a tombstone even after successful cleanup.
